# New Automated Tests

Page objects interact with the UI. Tests own assertions. Never hide, weaken, or skip a check to get a green run.

## Assertions belong in tests

No `assert` inside page objects (`pages/`). Expose locators, getters, and actions; the test asserts with pytest `assert` only. Never use Playwright `expect()`.

```python
# ❌ BAD — assertion inside the page object, or Playwright expect()
class LoginPage:
    def login_user(self, username: str, password: str):
        self.username.fill(username)
        self.password.fill(password)
        self.login_button.click()
        expect(self.page).to_have_url("**/inventory.html")

# ✅ GOOD — page object returns locators/state; the test uses pytest assert
class LoginPage:
    def login_user(self, username: str, password: str) -> InventoryPage:
        self.username.fill(username)
        self.password.fill(password)
        self.login_button.click()
        return InventoryPage(self.page)

    def get_error_message(self):
        return self.error_message

def test_locked_out_user_sees_error(login_page: LoginPage):
    login_page.login_user("locked_out_user", "secret_sauce")
    assert "locked out" in login_page.get_error_message().text_content()
```

## Never sleep; never Playwright `expect()`

Never `time.sleep()` or `page.wait_for_timeout()`. Never `expect()`. Locator actions and getters (`click`, `fill`, `text_content`, `inner_text`) auto-wait; then assert with pytest.

```python
# ❌ BAD
time.sleep(3)
expect(inventory_page.get_title()).to_have_text("Products")

# ✅ GOOD
assert inventory_page.get_title().text_content() == "Products"
assert inventory_page.get_title().is_visible()
```

## API tests use requests only

API tests and clients (`tests/api/`, `api/`) use the `requests` library only. Do not use Playwright `APIRequestContext`, `playwright.request`, or `expect()`. Assert with pytest on `status_code` and `response.json()`.

```python
# ❌ BAD — Playwright HTTP client
response = api_context.post("/booking", data=payload)
expect(response).to_be_ok()

# ✅ GOOD — requests session/client + pytest assert
response = booking_client.create_booking(payload)
assert response.status_code == 200
assert response.json()["bookingid"]
assert response.json()["booking"] == payload
```

## Never weaken a failing assertion

If a test fails, fix the app, locator, wait, or test data. Do not delete the assertion, skip the test to hide the failure, broaden the expected value, or replace a real `assert` with a no-op just to make the run pass.
